Logical operators are used to combine or negate boolean values:

- `&&`: logical AND
- `||`: logical OR
- `!`: logical NOT

```js
const a = true;
const b = false;
const c = a && b;   // false (both must be true)
const d = a || b;   // true (at least one must be true)
const e = !a;       // false (negates the value)
```

